link">801-237-2900</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@sltrib.com" class="contact-link">support@sltrib.com</a></p></div><div class="copy-container row hidden-md-down"><div class="col-12 col-md-6 logo-column"><a href="/"><img src="/pf/resources/svg/sltrib-logo.svg?d=646" alt="The Salt Lake Tribune Logo" width="250" height="46" class="trib-svg-white"/></a></div><div class="col-12 col-md-6 copy-column"><p class="copy">sltrib.com © 1996-<!-- -->2026 <!-- -->The Salt Lake Tribune. All rights reserved.</p></div></div><div class="hidden-md-up v-space mobile-copyright"><a href="/"><img src="/pf/resources/svg/Trib_masthead_top_000000.svg?d=646" alt="The Salt Lake Tribune Logo" width="300" height="46"/></a></div></div></div></footer></div></div><script id="fusion-metadata" type="application/javascript">window.Fusion=window.Fusion||{};Fusion.arcSite="sltrib";Fusion.contextPath="/pf";Fusion.mxId="00000000";Fusion.deployment="646";Fusion.globalContent={"_id":"UFR2UVAAZ5GPDFLNURYL5AA4YQ","additional_properties":{"has_published_copy":true,"is_published":true,"publish_date":"2025-06-30T20:40:33.091Z"},"address":{},"canonical_website":"sltrib","content_elements":[{"_id":"OLM5Y4VVQZEH5ONM5CVINFQMVE","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625306},"content":"","type":"text"},{"_id":"4LYEFZFM3FERTFED7YOCLJH4GM","additional_properties":{},"content":"Our Mission","level":4,"type":"header"},{"_id":"EVINY7SV6FDXBAQYDERDJZNEGM","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625308},"content":"<i>The Tribune is Utah’s independent voice. Building on a legacy of courageous, watchdog journalism, we strive to tell stories that are interesting, important and inclusive. Dedicated to fairness and accuracy, we aim to engage and empower you — our readers.</i>","type":"text"},{"_id":"MPW6JDV2UZAORGIGNPPKJGXLRA","content":"<div id=\"nonprofit\"></div>","type":"raw_html"},{"_id":"7J65WAFBGFB2ROWGO6HHHZDGDU","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625310},"content":"","type":"text"},{"_id":"56OA64GBZJF47JTAHKSLEWQ5TY","additional_properties":{},"content":"Our Nonprofit Model","level":4,"type":"header"},{"_id":"MS5JGAHQOJHOBFPCJCUTBX6AIY","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625312},"content":"In a historic move, the IRS approved a new nonprofit Salt Lake Tribune in October 2019, making it the first legacy newspaper in the U.S. to transform from a for-profit company to a 501(c)(3) nonprofit.","type":"text"},{"_id":"MKJ3CVPNIVDGBKG6CLURN2ZDBY","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625313},"content":"Under this new business model, The Tribune will continue to offer subscriptions and accept traditional advertising (although it will pay taxes on that income). But now, the newspaper can also receive donations — large and small — from donors who may receive a tax deduction for their donation. Since our approval, we’ve heard from hundreds of supporters from Utah and across the country, so thank you for the donations and encouragement!","type":"text"},{"_id":"54BJFDBVWZHJXAUNGWAJXHSP2M","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625314},"content":"On the editorial side, The Tribune will continue offering unmatched reporting on state and local government, politics, the environment, education, religion, criminal justice, sports and the variety of rich stories about the people and places that make Utah special. The only substantive change readers will notice is that The Tribune’s editorial board — which operates independently of the news staff — will no longer make candidate endorsements. Nonprofits can’t do that under federal law.","type":"text"},{"_id":"LLKLFY55YVEZXMFRRVPZZVKG3U","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625315},"content":"The Salt Lake Tribune is pioneering one path forward for local news. See our <a href=\"https://www.sltrib.com/about-us/annual-report/2025/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://www.sltrib.com/about-us/annual-report/2025/\">2025 Annual Report here</a>.","type":"text"},{"_id":"2VLVADJMFNEFRIHNUR2WZ5ND4A","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938882783},"content":"We’re also helping others who may be interested in converting a for-profit news organization into a nonprofit. <a href=\"https://playbook.sltrib.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"https://playbook.sltrib.com/\">See our playbook here. </a>","type":"text"},{"_id":"3UM6M4VEJND73ORBHJWPN4DHTU","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625316},"content":"Here are a few answers to key questions.","type":"text"},{"_id":"Z2WYHF5HTZA5BFZTRZZTLRPNOM","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625317},"content":"<b>I’m excited to support The Tribune! How can I donate?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"6SATFYD4YZGUDOMA7VTAYA3BNE","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625318},"content":"The Tribune is ready to accept your tax-deductible donation of any amount <a href=\"http://sltrib.com/giving\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"http://sltrib.com/giving\">here</a>. Prefer to mail a check? Our address is The Salt Lake Tribune, Inc., 48 West Market St., Suite 200, Salt Lake City, Utah, 84101.","type":"text"},{"_id":"5MQXD6ZSTNDUZHH66K36YNCUAE","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625325},"content":"<b>Will Tribune news stories change?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"D7YBFDJYWRFNREXP6EJEPPN5JU","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625326},"content":"While our business model is changing, our journalistic ethics and commitment to the highest quality journalism remain the same. We will always be Utah’s independent voice.","type":"text"},{"_id":"Y7BH5K4GHBBXRETZONWHVQWKDY","additional_properties":{},"content":"<b>Do you accept gifts from IRAs, stocks, or DAFs? Can I leave The Tribune in my will?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"YZJWNAMDPJCKBEYYKBKIKDF7MI","additional_properties":{},"content":"We accept all forms of gifts. To make a donation from a charitable fund, please use the tax ID number 84-1878709. You can find your DAF portal <a href=\"https://www.dafdirect.org/DAFDirect/daflink?_dafdirect_settings=ODQxODc4NzA5XzIxMTFfMThhOTA4NGEtMDYwMC00ZDVhLWJhOTItMzJkMDVhYmFlMTNm&amp;designatedText=V2hlcmUgaXQncyBuZWVkZWQgbW9zdC4=&amp;amountValue=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">here</a>. You can find more information on all the ways to give <a href=\"http://sltrib.com/giving\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">here</a> or please reach out to chief development officer Ciel Hunter at <a href=\"mailto:chunter@sltrib.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" title=\"mailto:chunter@sltrib.com\">chunter@sltrib.com</a>.","type":"text"},{"_id":"FHJD44N4ORFE3HVKF563WILLEI","additional_properties":{},"content":"<b>Who will own The Tribune now?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"PL7S6RLWLZBNNFGTOMK3DLTJGY","additional_properties":{},"content":"The nonprofit Tribune is not owned by any one person. A <a href=\"https://www.sltrib.com/board-and-advisers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">board of directors</a> has fiduciary responsibility for and governs The Tribune.","type":"text"},{"_id":"PTS2GW3HWFC3LIPCDFJDBXIX4U","additional_properties":{},"content":"Tom Love serves as chair of the board. Lauren Gustus is CEO and executive editor and oversees the newsroom. Our nonprofit bylaws create a strict firewall between the board and the newsroom, so Tribune reporters and editors remain free to report the news as they see fit by following the highest journalistic ethical standards.","type":"text"},{"_id":"72R37CTSRRB3HLL34WKHX4V65M","additional_properties":{},"content":"<b>Will board members have sway over what the paper covers?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"76UX7RG665AC7EKF3ZSIPGGTKE","additional_properties":{},"content":"The Tribune maintains firm separation between governing bodies and the newsroom. That means they will have no more access to the newsroom or influence on editorial decision-making than any other members of the public. The same rules apply to advertisers and sponsors, as has been our practice historically.","type":"text"},{"_id":"IXHLYZXXARBULLHALXSDC53BLM","additional_properties":{},"content":"<b>What about donors? Will they influence the content?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"S5UQI3UNWBG5VLHUCTOLZ4OB4U","additional_properties":{},"content":"No. While we will seek financial support for reporting and special projects, no donor or gift directs or influences the organization’s reporting on issues, people or organizations. We are committed to full transparency and understand this is fundamental to the trust our readers have in The Tribune. Our gift policy is found <a href=\"https://local.sltrib.com/nonprofit/sltrib_gift_policy.pdf?_gl=1*1rcdos3*_ga*NDk0ODA2NDAyLjE3NDQyMjg2MDc.*_ga_DC2TJEE08T*MTc0NDI0MTkyNi4yLjEuMTc0NDI0Njc1Mi40LjAuMA..\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">here</a>. Tribune supporters of over $5,000 are found <a href=\"https://www.sltrib.com/supporters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">here</a>.","type":"text"},{"_id":"2PXWIGTD2JFJLDN5QVJ3NIVG3Q","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625329},"content":"<b>Can I still advertise in the newspaper and on </b><a href=\"https://www.sltrib.com/\"><b>sltrib.com</b></a><b>?</b>","type":"text"},{"_id":"UOGTJHK7AZDUTH4VJFCP7Y2BJQ","additional_properties":{"_id":1728938625330},"content":"Yes. Please contact us at <a href=\"mailto: